From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:04:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: give the AVD its PMP
 performance request

Under macOS 26B123 on this machine the video decoder asks the PMP for
performance around its work: a hypervisor trace of 4K HEVC, H.264 and
AV1 decode shows power-request bit 20 (the AVD's position in the ADT's
soc-device table) set before a burst of jobs, SOC-DEV-DVFS entry 418
written with main level 2 while the AVD works and with level 0 after
it, and bit 20 cleared once it idles. Linux asks for nothing, and our
AVD takes about 6.8 ms per 4K HEVC frame against 2.7 ms on macOS.

Describe the request as a PMP report entry, the way T6000 does, and
make it the AVD's core power domain under its PMGR domain, so it is held
exactly while the decoder is runtime-active. macOS never reads the
acknowledge word and on this SoC the acknowledge bits do not follow the
request bits, so the entry does not wait for one.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 26 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index a5858080d6..10487f2140 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -1432,8 +1432,32 @@ pmc_soc_max: floor-soc-max {
 	};
 };
 
+/*
+ * The AVD's PMP performance request, as macOS 26B123 makes it on this machine
+ * (hypervisor trace of 4K HEVC/H.264/AV1 decode): power-request bit 20 (the
+ * AVD's position in the ADT's soc-device table) is set before each burst of
+ * decode jobs, SOC-DEV-DVFS entry 418 carries main level 2 while the AVD
+ * works, the level is written back to 0 first and bit 20 is cleared when it
+ * idles. macOS never reads the acknowledge word, and on this SoC its bits do
+ * not follow the request bits, so the entry does not wait for one.
+ */
+&pmp_report {
+	#address-cells = <1>;
+	#size-cells = <0>;
+
+	pmp_report_avd_sys: report@14 {
+		compatible = "apple,t6000-pmp-v2-report-entry";
+		reg = <0x14>;
+		label = "pmp-avd-sys";
+		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
+		power-domains = <&ps_avd_sys>;
+		apple,dvfs = <418 2>;
+		apple,no-ack;
+	};
+};
+
 &avd {
-	power-domains = <&ps_avd_sys>, <&pmc_soc_max>;
+	power-domains = <&pmp_report_avd_sys>, <&pmc_soc_max>;
 	power-domain-names = "core", "perf";
 };
 
